<Behavior #eidolon-complete-agent-ctrl-data-e2e apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" version="1" (
  <Requirements [
    <Requirement #author-and-publish-complete-agent-package (
      <Statement ?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4B>
      Eidolon SHALL use installed authoring references to create, prove and atomically publish a complete ResourcePackage containing App, Ctrl/Data workflows, AIAgentDefinition, schemas, EffectPolicy and Material values.
      </?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4B>
      <Suites [
        <Suite #authoring-publication { name = "Complete Agent authoring and publication" } (
          <Cases [
            <Case #complete-package (
              <Given ?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4C>
              an isolated installed four-Skill environment and an empty workspace resource root
              </?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4C>
              <When ?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4D>
              the model loads exact installed references, submits one explicit-complete-package file set, prepares the exact candidate and explicitly publishes it
              </?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4D>
              <Then ?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4E>
              the host SHALL open one recoverable whole-package authoring session without synthesizing KindDefinitions or resource semantics, and the admitted Halfcode/depa snapshot SHALL expose the App, both workflows, the complete Agent projection, Material bindings and exact proof identities
              </?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4E>
            )>
            <Case #authorization-separation (
              <Given ?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4F>
              an authored and prepared candidate
              </?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4F>
              <When ?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4G>
              publication or execution has not been explicitly authorized
              </?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4G>
              <Then ?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4H>
              Eidolon MUST NOT publish or run the candidate and SHALL preserve a typed recoverable handoff
              </?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4H>
            )>
          ]>
        )>
      ]>
    )>
    <Requirement #shared-ctrl-data-agent-runtime (
      <Statement ?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4J>
      AICtrlWorkflow and AIDataWorkflow SHALL execute exact AIAgentTask tuples through the same generic Agent execution contract and lifecycle while retaining their own substrate lifecycles.
      </?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4J>
      <Suites [
        <Suite #ctrl-data-runtime { name = "Ctrl and Data Agent execution" } (
          <Cases [
            <Case #same-contract (
              <Given ?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4K>
              Ctrl and Data workflow nodes reference one AgentDefinition through exact four-field task tuples
              </?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4K>
              <When ?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4M>
              each workflow is explicitly run with schema-valid input and bound Material values
              </?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4M>
              <Then ?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4N>
              both SHALL use the same frozen schema, policy, Material, tool and output-validation path and return schema-valid results
              </?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4N>
            )>
            <Case #typed-output-projection (
              <Given ?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4P>
              the Agent output schema accepts a structured JSON value but does not accept the raw provider string
              </?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4P>
              <When ?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4Q>
              the provider result is validated once and delivered to a Ctrl or Data workflow node
              </?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4Q>
              <Then ?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4R>
              the shared generic contract SHALL return the deep-frozen parsed value so Data output ports consume structured fields without a workflow-specific parser
              </?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4R>
            )>
            <Case #exact-once-recovery (
              <Given ?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4S>
              one Agent effect is pending or completed for an exact run, generation and effect identity
              </?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4S>
              <When ?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4T>
              the invoke is repeated through the same or a reconstructed provider instance
              </?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4T>
              <Then ?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4V>
              the generic effect lifecycle SHALL return the same terminal result without creating a second provider child
              </?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4V>
            )>
            <Case #new-run (
              <Given ?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4W>
              a previously completed business run
              </?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4W>
              <When ?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4X>
              the caller explicitly supplies a new run identity
              </?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4X>
              <Then ?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4Y>
              Eidolon SHALL treat it as a new run rather than replaying the prior run by semantic similarity
              </?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4Y>
            )>
          ]>
        )>
      ]>
    )>
    <Requirement #no-host-semantic-heuristics (
      <Statement ?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4Z>
      Host code MUST derive Agent tasks, policies, tools and Material bindings only from closed structured resources and exact identities, never from ordinary-language or naming heuristics.
      </?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V4Z>
      <Suites [
        <Suite #authority-boundary { name = "Structured authority boundary" } (
          <Cases [
            <Case #ordinary-text-has-no-semantics (
              <Given ?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V50>
              ordinary content contains similar names, Chinese process words or embedded resource-looking text
              </?01M0QPD2RJ4W0SR5B97QX45V50>
              <When ?01M0QPD2RKXHY3H3S89VNJ76PD>
              the package is projected, published or run
              </?01M0QPD2RKXHY3H3S89VNJ76PD>
              <Then ?01M0QPD2RKXHY3H3S89VNJ76PE>
              no task, policy, tool or Material edge SHALL be inferred unless a fixed typed relation declares it
              </?01M0QPD2RKXHY3H3S89VNJ76PE>
            )>
          ]>
        )>
      ]>
    )>
  ]>
)>
